{"id": "route-rag-014", "question": "Which waiting periods or exclusions apply to legal protection cover?", "subcategory": "legal_protection_exclusions", "expected_route": "retrieval_only", "actual_route": "retrieval_only", "status_code": 200, "latency_ms": 9883.5125, "evaluable": true, "route_correct": true, "operational_success": true, "answer": "The following waiting periods and exclusions apply to legal protection cover:\n\n- **Waiting Periods:**\n  - Legal dispute with an insurance company, health insurance fund, or pension fund: **3 months** (does not apply in connection with an accident) [legal-protection-sti.pdf, page 4].\n  - Legal disputes as a tenant with a landlord: **3 months** [legal-protection-sti.pdf, page 5].\n  - Civil disputes with neighbors: **3 months** [legal-protection-sti.pdf, page 5].\n\n- **Exclusions:**\n  - No legal protection is granted if the insured person has engaged in domain name grabbing [legal-protection-sti.pdf, page 4].\n  - The insurance does not cover the defense of the insured person against claims for damages or the enforcement of pure financial losses (in the absence of associated bodily injury or property damage) [legal-protection-sti.pdf, page 3].\n  - Costs will only be covered in the event of an acquittal or if the case is dropped if the insured person is investigated for a premeditated offense [legal-protection-sti.pdf, page 3].\n\nSource:\n- [legal-protection-sti.pdf, page 3]\n- [legal-protection-sti.pdf, page 4]\n- [legal-protection-sti.pdf, page 5]", "answer_present": true, "crm_fact_recall": null, "crm_reference_resolved": true, "crm_facts": [], "crm_checks": [], "requirement_recall": 0.5, "requirements": [{"id": "legal_waiting_period", "description": "Cases arising before contract conclusion or during an applicable waiting period are excluded.", "alternatives": ["before conclusion of the contract or during the waiting period", "cases arising during the waiting period are not covered", "pre existing legal disputes 